["I need to make 24 using 9, 5, 6, 3 with each number once.\n\nLet me try different combinations.\n\n9 + 5 + 6 + 3 = 23, no.\n9 + 5 + 6 - 3 = 17\n9 + 5 - 6 + 3 = 11\n9 - 5 + 6 + 3 = 13\n9 * 5 - 6 * 3 = 45 - 18 = 27\n9 * 5 - 6 - 3 = 45 - 9 = 36\n(9 - 5) * 6 = 24, then need to use 3... (9-5)*6*3 = 72, (9-5)*6/3 = 8, (9-5)*6+3 = 27, (9-5)*6-3 = 21\n(9 - 6) * (5 + 3) = 3 * 8 = 24! Let me check: 9-6=3, 5+3=8, 3*8=24. Yes!\n\nWait, but I used 3 twice? No: 9, 6, 5, 3. Each once. \n\n(9 - 6) * (5 + 3) = 3 * 8 = 24. \n\nLet me verify: 9, 6, 5, 3 - all four numbers used once. Yes!\n"]